---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const releases = [
  ['v0.5', 'Program Calendar', 'Understand work alongside leave, holidays, and program events.'],
  ['v0.6', 'Milestones & Deliveries', 'Track program outcomes and delivery readiness.'],
  ['v0.7', 'Communication', 'Share plans and reports outside the application.'],
  ['v0.8', 'Scenarios & Reconciliation', 'Compare alternatives and reconcile Jira changes.'],
  ['v0.9', 'Stabilisation', 'Improve reliability, usability, and desktop packaging.'],
  ['v1.0', 'Stable', 'Complete the import-to-planning-to-export workflow.'],
];
---

<Page title="Roadmap">
  <h1>Small releases. Useful progress.</h1>
  <p>This is a direction, not a delivery schedule. Planacity is a single-maintainer
    side project; scope stays focused on one useful increment at a time.</p>
  <h2>Current target: v0.4 - Team &amp; Capacity</h2>
  <p>Build toward realistic team capacity, starting with explicit work calendars.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Available: Timeline with day, week, and month scales</li>
    <li>Available: hierarchy, Epic, and WorkGroup grouping, filters, and dependency arrows</li>
    <li>Available: drag bar edges or edit dates with the keyboard without changing effort hours</li>
    <li>Available: named work calendars, person assignments, and dated availability with overlap previews</li>
    <li>Available: recurring-capacity wizard with per-person previews, overlaps, and overload warnings</li>
    <li>Planned: program-event deductions, work allocations, and allocation load checks</li>
    <li>Planned: <a href="https://github.com/tidus747/planacity/issues/65">Plan filters consistent with Timeline</a>, with safe hierarchy editing</li>
    <li>Implemented foundations: manual planning, Jira CSV roundtrip, and local persistence</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="status">This is a development preview. Available hours account for entered
    unavailability; the reservation wizard previews recurring duties before program
    events and work allocations.
    No stable release is published yet. Jira APIs and re-import reconciliation are deferred.</p>
  <h2>Later milestones</h2>
  <ul>
    {releases.map(([version, name, goal]) => <li><strong>{version} - {name}:</strong> {goal}</li>)}
  </ul>
</Page>
